  "B016_fusion": {
    "assessment_state": "unknown",
    "rationale": "Criterion requires at least two separately identified modalities in a fusion operation. The implemented correction combines MRI latents, longitudinal differences, MRI-derived core/ring occupancy and non-spatial context using projections and context modulation. Multiple timepoints and derived maps of MRI are not independent modalities. The observed acquisition/clinical context a_i is not enumerated enough to establish a distinct second modality in the evaluated configuration. Thus combined-input processing is explicit, but multimodal fusion under this criterion remains unresolved after source review, not unassessed or proven absent."
  },
